{"schemaVersion":2,"sectionID":20017673,"chapterID":15000204,"chapterNumber":"II-4","sectionNumber":"24-53","title":"Alternate Front Setbacks","officialText":"","previewText":"R6 R7 R8 R9 R10 R11 R12\n\nIn the districts indicated without a letter suffix, if an open area is provided along the full length of the front lot line with the minimum depth set forth in the following table, the provisions of Section 24-52 (Maximum Height of Walls and Required Setbacks) shall not apply. The minimum depth of such an open area shall be measured perpendicular to the front lot line. However, in such instan","blocks":[{"id":"zr-17673-block-001","kind":"html","html":"<p><span>R6 R7 R8 R9 R10 R11 R12</span></p>","plainText":"R6 R7 R8 R9 R10 R11 R12"},{"id":"zr-17673-block-002","kind":"html","html":"<p><span>In the districts indicated without a letter suffix, if an open area is provided along the full length of the <strong><em>front lot line</em></strong> with the minimum depth set forth in the following table, the provisions of Section <a class=\"sec-link-inline\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ii/chapter-4#24-52\" data-permitext-zr-source=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ii/chapter-4#24-52\"><span>24-52</span></a> (Maximum Height of Walls and Required Setbacks) shall not apply. The minimum depth of such an open area shall be measured perpendicular to the <strong><em>front lot line</em></strong>. However, in such instances, except as otherwise provided in Sections <a class=\"sec-link-inline\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ii/chapter-4#24-51\" data-permitext-zr-source=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ii/chapter-4#24-51\"><span>24-51</span></a> (Permitted Obstructions) or <a class=\"sec-link-inline\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ii/chapter-4#24-54\" data-permitext-zr-source=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ii/chapter-4#24-54\"><span>24-54</span></a> (Tower Regulations), no <strong><em>building or other structure</em></strong> shall penetrate the alternate <strong><em>sky exposure plane</em></strong> set forth in the table, and the <strong><em>sky exposure plane</em></strong> shall be measured from a point above the <strong><em>street line</em></strong>.</span></p>","plainText":"In the districts indicated without a letter suffix, if an open area is provided along the full length of the front lot line with the minimum depth set forth in the following table, the provisions of Section 24-52 (Maximum Height of Walls and Required Setbacks) shall not apply. The minimum depth of such an open area shall be measured perpendicular to the front lot line. However, in such instances, except as otherwise provided in Sections 24-51 (Permitted Obstructions) or 24-54 (Tower Regulations), no building or other structure shall penetrate the alternate sky exposure plane set forth in the table, and the sky exposure plane shall be measured from a point above the street line."},{"id":"zr-17673-block-003","kind":"html","html":"<p><span>If the open area provided under the terms of this Section is a <strong><em>public plaza</em></strong>, such open area may be counted for the bonus provided for a <strong><em>public plaza</em></strong> in the districts indicated in Section <a class=\"sec-link-inline\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ii/chapter-4#24-14\" data-permitext-zr-source=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ii/chapter-4#24-14\"><span>24-14</span></a> (Floor Area Bonus for a Public Plaza).</span></p>","plainText":"If the open area provided under the terms of this Section is a public plaza, such open area may be counted for the bonus provided for a public plaza in the districts indicated in Section 24-14 (Floor Area Bonus for a Public Plaza)."},{"id":"zr-17673-block-004","kind":"html","html":"<p><span>In R9 , R10, R11 or R12 Districts, the provisions of this Section shall be inapplicable to any <strong><em>development</em></strong> or <strong><em>enlargement</em></strong> with more than 25 percent of the total <strong><em>floor area</em></strong> of the <strong><em>building</em></strong> in <strong><em>residential use</em></strong>.</span></p>","plainText":"In R9 , R10, R11 or R12 Districts, the provisions of this Section shall be inapplicable to any development or enlargement with more than 25 percent of the total floor area of the building in residential use."},{"id":"zr-17673-block-005","kind":"html","html":"<p class=\"center-align\"><span>ALTERNATE REQUIRED FRONT SETBACKS</span></p>","plainText":"ALTERNATE REQUIRED FRONT SETBACKS"},{"id":"zr-17673-block-006","kind":"html","html":"<p><a id=\"t.8c0bb69ebeab4a79ae406291fb10ffcbd1798a1b\"></a><a id=\"t.9\"></a></p>","plainText":""},{"id":"zr-17673-block-007","kind":"table","html":"<table style=\"margin-left:auto;border-spacing:0;border-collapse:collapse;margin-right:auto\"><tbody><tr style=\"height:0pt\"><td colspan=\"2\" rowspan=\"3\" style=\"border-right-style:solid;padding:0pt 6pt 0pt 6pt;border-bottom-color:<strong><em>000000;border-top-width:0pt;border-right-width:0pt;border-left-color:</em></strong>000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:<strong><em>000000;border-left-width:0pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:127.5pt;border-top-color:</em></strong>000000;border-bottom-style:solid\">\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t<p><span>Depth of Optional Front Open Area<br>\n\t\t\t(in feet)</span></p>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"5\" rowspan=\"1\" style=\"border-right-style:solid;padding:0pt 6pt 0pt 6pt;border-bottom-color:<strong><em>000000;border-top-width:0pt;border-right-width:0pt;border-left-color:</em></strong>000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:<strong><em>000000;border-left-width:0pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:340.3pt;border-top-color:</em></strong>000000;border-bottom-style:soli